# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GENERATED by Terraform (infra/terraform/envs/local). DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
# Regenerated by `make dev` / `make reset`. Hand edits are overwritten.
# The authoritative var LIST lives in api/src/lib/env.ts (zod schema): add a
# var THERE and HERE together. This file holds dev/LocalStack VALUES only —
# never a real secret (LocalStack creds are the literal dummies "test").
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Auth (fake for local dev) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
AUTH_MODE=${auth_mode}
FAKE_USER_SUB=${fake_user_sub}

# ── Cognito (only used when AUTH_MODE=cognito, e.g. `make dev-snapshot`) ─────
# Public client identifiers (shipped in the SPA bundle) — not secrets.
COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=${cognito_user_pool_id}
COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=${cognito_client_id}
COGNITO_REGION=${cognito_region}

# ── Postgres (docker-compose container) ─────────────────────────────────────
DB_HOST=${db_host}
DB_PORT=${db_port}
DB_NAME=${db_name}
DB_USER=${db_user}
DB_PASSWORD=${db_password}

# ── LocalStack (AWS_ENDPOINT_URL routes all SDK calls to :4566) ─────────────
AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=${aws_endpoint_url}
AWS_REGION=${aws_region}
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=${aws_access_key_id}
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=${aws_secret_access_key}

# ── S3 buckets (provisioned into LocalStack by Terraform) ───────────────────
S3_BUCKET_MEDIA=${s3_bucket_media}
S3_BUCKET_TOPO=${s3_bucket_topo}
SVTM_FORMATION_S3_PATH=${svtm_formation_s3_path}

# ── App ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=${port}
NODE_ENV=${node_env}
CORS_ORIGIN=${cors_origin}
SES_FROM_EMAIL=${ses_from_email}
TOPO_CDN_BASE_URL=${topo_cdn_base_url}

# ── Snapshot (only for `make snapshot`) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Prod RDS creds are NOT stored here (they would be overwritten on regenerate
# and must not live in a tracked-shaped file). Export them in your shell or a
# separate gitignored file before running `make snapshot`:
#   DB_HOST_PROD= DB_NAME_PROD= DB_USER_PROD= DB_PASSWORD_PROD=
